rsion** is to provide the raw latent to the sampler. This is the way you can provide the raw latent as an input condition."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Note: Raw latent version", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [310, 150], "pos": [-590, 1430], "id": 388, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 3}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["[Tutorial](https://docs.comfy.org/tutorials/image/qwen/qwen-image-edit) | [教程](https://docs.comfy.org/zh-CN/tutorials/image/qwen/qwen-image-edit)\n\n\n## Model links\n\nWith the All-In-One model, all you need is this one model, which is convenient. \n\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\n- [Qwen-Rapid-AIO-NSFW-v5.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Phr00t/Qwen-Image-Edit-Rapid-AIO/blob/main/v5/Qwen-Rapid-AIO-NSFW-v5.safetensors)\nor\n- [Qwen-Rapid-AIO-SFW-v5.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Phr00t/Qwen-Image-Edit-Rapid-AIO/blob/main/v5/Qwen-Rapid-AIO-SFW-v5.safetensors)\n\nNote: the NSFW model is extremely horny, all ladies generated will not wear panties. Take note and/or rejoice.\n\n\n## Model Storage Location\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n└── 📂 models/\n     └── 📂 checkpoints/\n          |── Qwen-Rapid-AIO-NSFW-v5.safetensors\n          |   or\n          └── Qwen-Rapid-AIO-NSFW-v5.safetensors\n\n```\n"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Model links", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [539.5120239257812, 341.55108642578125], "pos": [-819.5120239257812, 1634.3873291015625], "id": 99, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 4}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Character image:\nThe character should be forward-facing, and ideally with the full body visible. Otherwise its very flexible. A-pose or T-pose are not necessary.\n\nThe generated image WILL attempt to adapt to the background. Its best that the character and pose images have similar camera angles.\n\nQwen is very adaptable to a humanoid of any style.\n\nPose image:\nThe character should be forward-facing or side-facing, and MUST be entirely visible. The character should not be upside-down, if so, flip it over.\n\nDW Pose is the issue here, it has a hard time recognizing weird poses and odd angles. It leans towards photo-real lighting, so take note.\n\nOtherwise, Qwen does a good job. If you have a method of manually providing a DW Pose formatted pose image, that will work even better"], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownNote", "title": "Character and Pose input images", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#653", "size": [310, 150], "pos": [-590, 2136.47412109375], "id": 417, "properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}}, "order": 5}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "IMAGE", "links": [653, 663], "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}], "size": [270, 82], "pos": [-211.40811157226562, 2499.27294921875], "widgets_values": ["nearest-exact", 1.5], "inputs": [{"name": "image", "link": 652, "label": "图像", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "图像"}, {"widget": {"name": "upscale_method"}, "name": "upscale_method", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "缩放方法"}, {"widget": {"name": "megapixels"}, "name": "megapixels", "type": "FLOAT", "localized_name": "像素数量"}], "flags": {}, "id": 414, "type": "ImageScaleToTotalPixels", "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.3.65", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "ImageScaleToTotalPixels"}, "order": 13}, {"outputs": [], "color": "#432", "widgets_values": ["Character image:\nSet to 1.0 - 1.5 Megapixels, depends on what your system can handle.\n\nAny lower will lower quality,\nany higher may lower quality.\n\nThe actual input image should be bigger than those numbers, if possible.\n\nIf its already in that range, you can disable the Scale node.\n\nPose image:\nDW Pose is pretty resource lite, so anything will do. However, it should approx be the same size or bigger than the character image.\n\nDefault of 1536 should be enough."], "inputs": [], "flags": {}, "type": "MarkdownN